      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "An inner product on $V={R}^{3}$ is given by $⟨x,y⟩=2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+5{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+7{x}_{3}{y}_{3}.$ Find $⟨x,y⟩$, if\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Computing the inner product according to the definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y⟩ & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+5{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+7{x}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 2\\cdot 3+5\\cdot 1\\cdot (-3)+7\\cdot (-2)\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =12-15+28 \\\\  & =25.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
